DISCLOSURE

Package:  @dhicoc/dsh-reverse-skill
Purpose:  DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugin that packages the upstream reverse-skill
          skill pack (87 SKILL.md documents) as a Cordis skill provider.
Upstream: https://github.com/zhaoxuya520/reverse-skill (MIT)

1. NATURE OF THE CONTENT

This package is a documentation-and-reference distribution. It contains:

  - 87 SKILL.md instruction documents covering reverse engineering,
    penetration testing, CTF, binary / firmware / mobile / JavaScript
    analysis, malware analysis, threat intelligence and exploit-chain
    reasoning;
  - supporting reference material, including an inert JSON catalogue of
    web-injection test payload strings and accompanying technique notes;
  - auxiliary helper scripts (PowerShell, POSIX shell and Python) that act as
    thin wrappers around well-known, independently distributed security tools
    such as apktool, jadx, Frida, IDA Pro and radare2.

The only first-party executable code is a small TypeScript provider
(~150 lines, shipped as lib/index.js) that reads the bundled SKILL.md files
from local disk and registers their name, description and body with the dsh
skill registry. It performs no other work.

2. WHY THIS IS DUAL-USE

The techniques and reference data bundled here serve legitimate defensive and
offensive security work, and could equally be misused. Automated scanning may
reasonably flag this material as resembling malware. It is nonetheless a
legitimate, publicly sourced security-research skill pack, distributed for
authorized use.

3. INTENDED LEGITIMATE USE

  - Authorized penetration testing and red-team engagements;
  - CTF competitions and isolated lab environments;
  - Security research, vulnerability discovery and coordinated disclosure;
  - Malware analysis, digital forensics and incident response;
  - Security education and professional training.

4. AUTHORIZATION REQUIREMENT

Users must apply these skills and scripts only against systems they own or for
which they hold explicit, documented authorization. Users are solely
responsible for complying with applicable law, engagement scope and rules of
engagement, and for maintaining audit logging appropriate to their
environment. Unauthorized use is neither intended nor supported.

5. SAFETY CHARACTERISTICS

  - No install-time execution. package.json declares no preinstall, install,
    postinstall or prepare hook. Installing this package from npm executes
    nothing.
  - No compiled artifacts. The package contains no .exe, .dll, .so, .elf,
    .bin or other binary files. It ships text files only.
  - No autonomous behavior. Nothing in this package opens network
    connections, contacts command-and-control infrastructure, establishes
    persistence, escalates privileges or accesses credentials. The plugin
    only reads local Markdown files.
  - Scripts are inert until explicitly invoked. The bundled helper scripts run
    only when a user deliberately executes them, and they merely drive the
    third-party tools listed in section 1. This package itself performs no
    automated scanning, exploitation or lateral movement, and therefore
    imposes no rate limiting of its own.
  - Documented, unmodified upstream provenance. All bundled content
    originates from the public, MIT-licensed reverse-skill project and is
    redistributed without modification.

6. REPORTING AND CONTACT

Security concerns, false-positive questions or abuse reports:
